# Windows scripts ship in the release zip and run under cmd.exe / PowerShell 5.1.
# HARD-WON: cmd.exe can mis-parse goto/call labels in LF-only .cmd files depending on
# where the label lands in the file (byte offset mod 512), so an unrelated edit can
# silently break "Install TrontSnap.cmd". Pin CRLF in the checkout whatever
# core.autocrlf says; the index stays LF, so diffs and Linux checkouts are unchanged.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
